<p>Note- Full name, Fletcher Energy. Market expectations were for a net profit of NZ$260 million. The result included a number of one-off items, being the NZ$32 million gain on the sale of its stake in Bay of Plenty Electricity and $37 million arising from the reduction in the carrying value of the Mobil Royalty liability. These were offset, in part, by a NZ$30 million writedown of the Flour Bluff (Texas) assets.  </p>
